# DNA-AND content · the grand tour: one flight from the whole visible universe down to the quarks, for watching
# Run it: Universe.exe --tour grand-tour (or DNA-AND.exe --tour grand-tour). Any key or click takes the controls back.
# Edit the stops to make your own. Each @stop leave
do: zoom
rate: -0.3
until-km: 5e21
caption: Every point of light out here is a whole galaxy

@stop web
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 10
caption: The cosmic web: galaxies along filaments, round vast empty voids

@stop choose-galaxy
do: pick
target: galaxy
caption: A galaxy

@stop to-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 1.5e18
caption: We fall toward one galaxy among a hundred billion

@stop round-galaxy
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 8e17
turn: 3
seconds: 10
caption: A hundred billion stars round a giant black hole

@stop into-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 1e16
caption: Into it: the glow breaks into stars, each a sun

@stop choose-star
do: pick
target: star
caption: A star

@stop into-system
do: zoom
rate: 0.6
until-km: 3e9
caption: One star, and the worlds born round it

@stop round-system
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Each world on its own tilted orbit

@stop planet-1
do: pick
target: next-planet
caption: One of its worlds

@stop to-planet-1
do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 1e5
caption: Across to one of its worlds

@stop round-planet-1
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Round it: a world of its own make

@stop star-2
do: pick
target: star
caption: Another star

@stop to-star-2
do: zoom
rate: 0.6
until-km: 3e9
caption: Across light-years to another star and its worlds

@stop round-star-2
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Another system, its worlds on their own orbits

@stop choose-planet
do: pick
target: planet
caption: A world

@stop to-planet
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 2e4
caption: Down to one of its worlds

@stop round-planet
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 1.5e4
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Seas, land, clouds and a thin shell of air

@stop to-land
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 1.5
caption: Down through the air to the land

@stop over-hills
do: glide
rate: 0.5
turn: 1.5
seconds: 12
caption: Hills raised by moving plates, valleys worn by water

@stop to-head-height
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 0.002
caption: Down to where a person stands

@stop stand
do: pick
target: none
caption: Standing

@stop look-up
do: look
tilt: 55
turn: 1.5
seconds: 6
caption: Look up

@stop sky
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 7
caption: Our star, the other worlds, the galaxy's stars beyond

@stop look-down
do: look
tilt: -85
turn: 1
seconds: 6
caption: And down: there is as much below us as above

@stop to-grains
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 2e-6
caption: The ground breaks into stones, then grains of sand

@stop to-face
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 2e-9
caption: Onto one grain, a crystal of one mineral

@stop round-face
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 6
caption: Its face: steps, cracks, clay plates, a film of water

@stop to-crystal
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 6e-12
caption: Down to its atoms

@stop round-crystal
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 6
caption: Atoms in a pattern repeated billions of times

@stop choose-atom
do: pick
target: atom
caption: One atom

@stop to-atom
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-13
caption: An atom is not a ball

@stop round-atom
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 2.5e-13
turn: 2.5
seconds: 8
caption: A tiny nucleus, its electrons round it on tilted paths

@stop to-neighbour
do: pick
target: bonded-atom
caption: Its neighbour

@stop across-bond
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 8
caption: Atoms share outer electrons: that glow is the bond

@stop choose-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: One electron

@stop follow-electron
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 6
caption: An electron: a point, and a wave spread through its cloud

@stop next-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: The next

@stop follow-next
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 6
caption: Each in its own orbital

@stop choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Inward: an atom is almost all empty space

@stop round-nucleus
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 1.2e-17
turn: 2.5
seconds: 8
caption: Protons and neutrons, bound by the strong force

@stop choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: A proton

@stop to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a single proton

@stop round-proton
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 8
caption: Three quarks in a storm of gluons

@stop choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: A quark

@stop to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-19
caption: One quark

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 1.5
seconds: 8
caption: The smallest thing we know. The same universe at every scale
